WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.880
If you're a solo or small real estate investor,

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:04.500
your deals are everywhere.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.840
Your inbox, your downloads, your texts.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.480
And every OM is written by a broker trying to sell,

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.360
each with its own level of optimism.

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:14.640
Before you ever underwrite a deal, you have to screen it.

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:18.120
Open the OM, pull the numbers, rebuild the rent roll,

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.160
compare it to everything else on your desk.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.480
ScoreOM handles that front end,

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:25.080
so you only spend real time on the deals that deserve it.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:28.720
Upload an OM, and in about a minute you get a score,

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:31.720
a plain-English brief, and the rent roll in Excel.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:33.480
That used to be 30 minutes to an hour

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.800
of retyping rent rolls and financials,

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:38.200
just to decide if a deal was worth a closer look.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.240
Now your first look takes about a minute.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.480
Then it runs every deal through the same criteria

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:44.860
and the same models, so you get a truer view

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:46.760
of how each one stacks up

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:48.840
against the other deals you've received.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:50.880
Every deal lands on a DealBoard.

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:53.920
Sort by score, cap rate, or NOI,

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.120
and see them all on a map.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:56.960
It also keeps deals moving.

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:59.920
Standing at a property and a partner asks how it looks?

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:02.080
Send the whole breakdown from your phone.

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:04.520
One link, no login.

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:06.180
And when a deal catches your eye,

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:07.600
give it more to work with.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:10.120
Add the trailing 12-month profit and loss,

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:12.360
a rent roll or lease abstracts,

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:13.560
and the read gets sharper.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:15.320
It won't replace your underwriting.

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:17.600
It just gets you to the right deals faster,

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:19.160
so your time goes where it counts.

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:20.900
Try it on your next OM.
